00:29:48.000 --> 00:30:24.000
validating where you might be coming from, but I also have needs as a parent and our environment has needs and rules that need to be followed. But slowing down is the main advice that I have for parents with children with sensitive temperament. The time that you take to slow down in the moment today, you're going to save 100-fold over in years to come when you're avoiding inpatient treatment and all the kind of crises that go with a young person with BPD. Does that same approach work with an adult who has BPD?

